          "id": "finding_6cfa859f891de75468793b0f7c26",
          "summary": "Procedural assessment: The excerpt identifies Flopsy, Mopsy, Cotton-tail, and Peter as four siblings living with their mother beneath a fir-tree. Their mother warns them away from Mr. McGregor’s garden, where their father had an accident, then leaves. While the three siblings gather berries, Peter enters the garden, eats vegetables, is chased by Mr. McGregor, loses his shoes and jacket, hides, becomes lost, and eventually escapes to the wood and returns home. He is tired and unwell; his mother puts him to bed and gives him camomile tea, while his siblings have bread, milk, and blackberries for supper. Requested elements covered: family relationships and principal events in the supplied excerpt. Residuals: none for this topic within the excerpt; events beyond it are not established.",
